# Docker build-context excludes for the backend image.
#
# Context is the backend/ directory (see backend/Dockerfile). The Dockerfile
# does `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked into the image.
#
# Runtime NEEDS (do NOT add these): app/, alembic/, alembic.ini, pyproject.toml,
# uv.lock. The lifespan hook reads Config("alembic.ini") + alembic/versions/**,
# and the uv build backend packages the `app` module. Keep all of them.

# --- R15: never bake local secrets / env files into the image ---
# The container gets its config from Fly secrets / env at runtime, never from a
# committed .env. Exclude every concrete .env file, including the *.example ones
# (the build does not use them).
.env
.env.*

# --- Python virtualenv (rebuilt inside the image by `uv sync`) ---
.venv/

# --- Python caches / compiled artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Tests are not needed at runtime (image is built --no-dev) ---
tests/

# --- VCS metadata ---
.git/
.gitignore

# --- Docs (not referenced by pyproject/build) ---
*.md

# --- Docker artifacts themselves ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
